{
 "about": "C++ reduction against independent Orekit frames; 1 mm target at LEO/GEO, no tolerance widened. Before: untouched 1.3.1 native. After: current native (baseline mode repeats before).",
 "units": "Rotation angle mas; worst-direction displacement mm at LEO=6778137 m and GEO=42164170 m.",
 "notes": {
  "classical": "Orekit MODProvider composes the IERS 1996 psi_A/omega_A/chi_A cubic precession polynomials; ERFA pmat76 uses the IAU 1976 zeta/z/theta cubic parameterization. Their finite polynomial representations differ beyond their retained order. Orekit IERS 1996 nutation arguments also differ from ERFA IAU 1980 (documented in the pinned jar resource); measured ERFA/Orekit rows isolate that model spread.",
  "itrf": "Orekit minimum degree-3 EOP interpolation differs from FFM linear interpolation; same-EOP and interpolation-spread rows isolate it. Midnight rows land exactly on EOP records.",
  "clock": "LEO400 F3 samples are the August 25-epoch set. AlignedEop rows are explicitly diagnostic: R_ERFA(linear case EOP) * transpose(R_ERFA(Orekit cubic EOP)) * R_Orekit removes only the independently measured EOP interpolation effect. Raw Orekit rows are retained with the unchanged 1 mm target."
 },
